-- Comment sync observability.
--
-- SocialAccount.lastCommentSyncAt already existed in schema.prisma but no
-- code read or wrote it -- confirmed 2026-11-06, all 10 production accounts
-- NULL. Combined with comment-monitor.worker.ts logging only failures, that
-- left no way to tell a healthy fleet with nothing to collect apart from a
-- fleet consuming nothing at all. Answering "is comment ingestion working?"
-- took a full day across Netlify, Railway, Upstash and Postgres; with these
-- two columns written it is one query.
--
-- Hand-written rather than generated by `prisma migrate dev`, per
-- prisma/migrations/README.md: the direct connection Prisma Migrate needs
-- (DIRECT_URL, port 5432) is not reachable from the dev machine, only the
-- pooled DATABASE_URL (6543). Apply via the Supabase SQL Editor, then fold
-- into a real migration file from an environment that can reach DIRECT_URL.
--
-- Safe to re-run: every statement is guarded.

-- Null means the last attempt succeeded. Deliberately a free-text message
-- rather than an enum: the useful content is the provider's own wording
-- (e.g. Zernio's PLATFORM_NOT_SUPPORTED, or a token failure), which no
-- fixed set would have anticipated.
ALTER TABLE "SocialAccount"
  ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS "lastCommentSyncError" TEXT;

-- NOT backfilled. Every existing row is NULL for lastCommentSyncAt because
-- nothing ever wrote it, and inventing a timestamp would assert a sync that
-- never happened. The first tick after deploy populates them truthfully.
